  "summary": "If BIND is loaded with a \"`named.conf`\" file that contains no global \"`options`\" block, an attacker can send a query of…",
  "details": "If BIND is loaded with a \"`named.conf`\" file that contains no global \"`options`\" block, an attacker can send a query of QTYPE TKEY which may cause an assertion failure and subsequent unexpected program exit.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.",
